This is a miscompilation bug in VectorCombine.
Issue title: [VectorCombine] UB triggered after optimization
Detailed information:
BUG TYPE:
    miscompilation

VERIFICATION RESULT:
    Invalid refinement in @PR115575 -- Source is more defined than target

VIOLATED PROPERTY:
    UB refinement

SOURCE (pre-transformation IR):
target datalayout = "e-m:e-p270:32:32-p271:32:32-p272:64:64-i64:64-i128:128-f80:128-n8:16:32:64-S128"
target triple = "x86_64-unknown-unknown"
define <2 x i8> @PR115575(i8 %x) {
  %ins = insertelement <2 x i8> poison, i8 %x, i32 3
  %bo = sdiv <2 x i8> %ins, <i8 5, i8 2>
  ret <2 x i8> %bo
}

TARGET (post-transformation IR):
; ModuleID = '<stdin>'
source_filename = "<stdin>"
target datalayout = "e-m:e-p270:32:32-p271:32:32-p272:64:64-i64:64-i128:128-f80:128-n8:16:32:64-S128"
target triple = "x86_64-unknown-unknown"

define <2 x i8> @PR115575(i8 %x) {
  %bo.scalar = sdiv i8 %x, poison
  %bo = insertelement <2 x i8> poison, i8 %bo.scalar, i64 3
  ret <2 x i8> %bo
}

WHAT THE TRANSFORMATION CHANGED:
  modified:
    %bo
      source: %bo = sdiv <2 x i8> %ins, <i8 5, i8 2>
      target: %bo = insertelement <2 x i8> poison, i8 %bo.scalar, i64 3
  only in target:
    %bo.scalar: %bo.scalar = sdiv i8 %x, poison
  only in source:
    %ins: %ins = insertelement <2 x i8> poison, i8 %x, i32 3

CRITICAL VALUES:
    %bo
    %bo.scalar
    %ins

DEPENDENCY CHAIN (source):
    %ins = insertelement <2 x i8> poison, i8 %x, i32 3
    %bo = sdiv <2 x i8> %ins, <i8 5, i8 2>

CONTROL FLOW (blocks entered by the failing execution):
    (none)

COUNTEREXAMPLE INPUT:
    i8 %x = poison

DIVERGENCE (source vs target on that input):
    %bo.scalar: source = (not computed)   target = UB triggered!

INTERPRETATION:
    A transformation may not introduce undefined behaviour. Any execution that is UB-free in the source must remain UB-free in the target.
    The earliest reported divergence is at %bo.scalar.

